      "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
      "revision": 1328540059,
      "text": "Acacia colei, commonly known as Cole's wattle, kalkardi, candelabra wattle or soap wattle, is a species of flowering plant in the family Fabaceae. It forms a spreading shrub or tree with narrowly elliptic, more or less straight phyllodes, spikes of golden yellow flowers, and openly and strongly curved, thinly leathery to crust-like, more or less glabrous pods."
    }
